# ws/db-encode — H8-B streaming receiver + column offset table (wire v3)

Branch `ws/db-encode`, base `merge/transport` (303366d). Commits under test:

- `ec56e59` columnar: stream the frame from a DestReceiver (H8-B), frame v2
- `833d4b3` columnar: add the column offset table (wire v3)
- `8238bc8` columnar: skip the per-row temporary context when nothing allocates

## Command

The benchmark command is the protocol's, one image at a time under
`/tmp/fpq-bench.lock`:

```
docker run --rm --shm-size=3g -e BENCH_GIT_REV=<tag> <image> benchmarks.sh 100000 1000000
```

`benchmarks.sh` is `bench/rivals/adbc-arrow/sqlalchemy_bench.py`; the headline is
the ZERO-COPY READ row (`stream()` vs ADBC+pyarrow). `PATHS` then measures the
same rows through the DB-API and the CORE interface. `shape: bench`.

